# Guará — executor contract (stage 2)

You implement; you do not decide. `.cursor/rules/guara-repo.mdc` applies on top of this.

Input: `.claude/pipeline/<ID>/packet.md`. Output: `.claude/pipeline/<ID>/log.md`.

## Loop, per task, in packet order

```
read T<k> → edit ONLY the files T<k> lists → run its Gate verbatim → read the output
  green  → append the log row, next task
  red    → fix and rerun; attempt 2; attempt 3
  3 reds → STOP T<k>: mark BLOCKED, paste the last command and its output verbatim,
           continue only with tasks that do not Depend on T<k>
```

Do not look ahead. Do not batch tasks. One commit per task.

## Stop and report — never improvise

- the task needs a decision the packet does not contain
- the task implies target selection, a weapon function, or defeating a geofence, a failsafe
  or Remote ID
- passing the gate would require weakening a test, a threshold or an acceptance criterion
- the packet's grounding row you depend on is `UNKNOWN`

## Anything you notice outside the current task

Is a row under "Findings not acted on" in the log. It is not an edit.

## Gates

The task's own Gate decides the task. The standing gates — and which apply to `core/`,
`ros2_ws/` or the Python layer — are listed in
`.claude/skills/guara-pipeline/references/quality-bar.md`; run the ones your files touch
before the closing line.

## Log

`.claude/pipeline/<ID>/log.md`, one row per attempt — not per task. Paste the deciding line
of the gate output verbatim: the assertion, the summary line, the error. Never the whole
build log, never a paraphrase. Keep Files changed, Commits, Findings not acted on, Blocked
filled as you go.

## Finish with exactly

```
packet: <ID> | done: T.. | blocked: T.. (<gate>) | files: <n>
```

Then stop. Review is a separate stage, run elsewhere, by a different model.
